* CABSRT12 - PRINT STREAM SORT FOR THE BURST SEQUENCE
* THE INSERTER TAKES THE PRINT STREAM IN MAIL SORT ORDER, NOT IN
* ACCOUNT ORDER.  THIS SORT PUTS IT IN ZIP CODE ORDER USING THE
* E15 EXIT TO PULL THE ZIP OFF THE INVOICE HEADER LINE, WHICH IS
* THE ONLY LINE IN THE STREAM THAT CARRIES IT.
*
* THE EXIT ALSO SUPPRESSES ANY DOCUMENT WHOSE FIRST LINE CARRIES
* A CARRIAGE CONTROL OTHER THAN 7.  THAT IS HOW A PARTIALLY
* FORMATTED INVOICE IS KEPT OUT OF THE MAIL RUN.  NOTHING IN THE
* FORMAT FAMILY IS AWARE OF THIS.
 SORT FIELDS=(1,20,CH,A)
 MODS E15=(CABSXZIP,4096,SORTEXIT,N),E35=(CABSXBST,2048,SORTEXIT,N)
 OPTION EQUALS
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=133
